WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.250
Next question is about Andrew Yang.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:08.700
Hey David, when will Andrew Yang entered the
top three Democratic primary candidates in

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.970
the polling?

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:14.830
So I'm going to assume that this is a serious
question because the person who sent it has

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:20.850
been emailing me about Andrew Yang in a perfectly
reasonable and serious manner for a year and

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.910
they genuinely seem to be fans and supporters
of Andrew Yang.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.280
I'm not going to assume it's a trolling question,
but here's the deal.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.529
Andrew Yang is not going to enter the top
three in 2020 democratic polling and that's

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:32.529
okay.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:33.529
All right.

00:00:33.529 --> 00:00:36.660
He's done way more than many people expected.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:42.750
He has introduced some interesting ideas into
the 2020 democratic primary discussion.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.210
Now I know a lot of people will say, David,
stop it.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:52.469
Andrew has said his goal is not pull 3% his
goal is to be president of the United States.

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:53.549
That's great.

00:00:53.549 --> 00:00:54.809
That should be everyone's goal.

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:55.809
Who's running for president?

00:00:55.809 --> 00:01:00.369
I wish everybody was genuinely running because
they believe that they are going to be president

00:01:00.369 --> 00:01:01.609
of the United States.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:03.379
I have no problem with Andrew and personally.

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:04.379
I like him.

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:06.140
I've interviewed him multiple times.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.540
I see him as sincere.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.610
I see him as genuine.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.740
I don't see him as some kind of right Libertarian
Trojan horse.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.470
As some people have pointed out, he has policy
ideas.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.470
Some are better than others.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:20.990
There are problems with some of his policy
ideas and that's all as we would expect with

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:26.520
any candidate, but he's not going to pull
in the top three and it's not because I don't

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.020
believe in him.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.020
Okay.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:34.320
Andrew Yang was in sixth place heading into
the third debate last night behind Biden,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.270
Bernie, Warren Harris and Buddha judge.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.820
It is already a huge accomplishment that he's
ahead of all sorts of actual elected officials

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.260
and political insiders.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:50.170
He's ahead of Beto and Cory booker and Tulsi
Gabbert and numerous other members of Congress

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.330
and more establishment people who had higher
name recognition at the beginning of this

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.330
campaign.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:59.190
Now maybe I'll be eating my hat next week
if new posts, debate polling shows Andrew

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:05.330
Yang in third place, but between Biden and
Bernie and Warren, that's roughly two thirds

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.000
of the Democratic primary electorate already.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.310
If you look at their second choices, I don't
see a mathematical path for Andrew Yang to

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:16.849
break the top three.

00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:22.069
Even if everyone other than Biden, Bernie
and Warren drops out and Andrew Yang gets

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:28.060
a full 50% of all of that support of all those
other people.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.680
That's 11 points.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.920
It's still not enough to break into third
place and that's not even accounting for the

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:39.159
reality that the support of some of those
other candidates would go to Bernie Biden

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:44.159
and Warren making it even more difficult for
Andrew Yang to catch up so he's not going

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:47.189
to enter the top three in this election.

00:02:47.189 --> 00:02:49.750
That doesn't mean he can't have an impact.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.590
It doesn't mean he's a bad person.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:53.549
It doesn't mean he's running a bad campaign.

00:02:53.549 --> 00:02:57.579
He has ideas, some of which are good and some
of which are less good like any candidate

00:02:57.579 --> 00:02:59.930
and that's all great.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.319
But if people are genuinely waiting for the
day in which we say Andrew Yang has pulled

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:06.689
into second place, I don't see it happening.

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:12.660
If you disagree with me, give me the mathematical
path that Andrew Yang has, not just, he's

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:18.139
gonna just crush it, uh, between now and election
day and the first primaries and he'll be in

00:03:18.139 --> 00:03:19.609
second or third place before you know it.

00:03:19.609 --> 00:03:20.789
I just don't see it convinced me that I'm
wrong.

